      "details": "<p>A square defensive tower about 20 meters high, it dates to the period of the Saracen invasions of Italy and is built atop the remains of a Roman villa. The tower was one of a group of defensive coastal towers built in the eighth and ninth centuries. It was restored in 1562.</p>",
